@prefix grlife: <https://w3id.org/kee/lifecycle/governance-record#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

# The review status of a governance record.
#
# Four Draft profiles require kee:lifecycleState on records that are about
# governing knowledge rather than knowledge themselves: governance transition
# records (including multi-typed authority and promotion records),
# contradiction records, contested authority claims and lifecycle crosswalk
# mappings. The value on that slot is the record's own standing as a record:
# whether it has been proposed, accepted, rejected, withdrawn or superseded by
# whatever review governs records of its kind. It is not the state of anything
# the record describes.
#
# Owner: the Governance Transition Profile. Adopted, by name, for
# kee:lifecycleState on kee:GovernanceTransitionRecord (owner, including
# multi-typed kee:AuthorityRecord and kee:PromotionRecord),
# kee:ContradictionRecord (Contradiction Records Profile),
# kee:ContestedAuthorityClaim (Authority and Delegation Profile) and
# kee:LifecycleCrosswalkMapping (Lifecycle Crosswalk Profile). It is not
# adopted for kee:AssertionMetadataRecord, whose slot carries the lifecycle of
# the managed assertion unit, drawn from the scheme of the profile governing
# that unit (https://w3id.org/kee/lifecycle/assertion# when no other does).
#
# What this axis must not carry, because each has its own carrier already:
#   1. a dispute's resolution or disposition (kee:resolutionOutcome where used,
#      Section 13.1): an Accepted contradiction record is an accepted record
#      of a conflict, not a resolved conflict;
#   2. a grant's expiry, revocation or suspension (kee:validUntil,
#      prov:invalidatedAtTime; Section 12.2): a revoked grant's record normally
#      stays Accepted, because revocation is an event and not a rejection of
#      the record;
#   3. the recorded or target state (kee:previousLifecycleState,
#      kee:newLifecycleState, kee:lifecycleStatusVocabulary on a transition
#      record; the source and target terms on a crosswalk record; Section 9.4);
#   4. mapping strength (the SKOS mapping relation; Section 9.4): accepting a
#      crosswalk record does not upgrade a close, broad, narrow or related
#      match to an exact one;
#   5. epistemic standing, confidence, authority or correctness (Sections 9.1,
#      11 and 12.5): Supported, Qualified, Challenged, a confidence value, a
#      claim of authority.
#
# Transition constraints: none. The scheme defines no state machine and no
# permitted orderings. History: a change of a record's review status does not
# erase the earlier value or its provenance; it is recorded by a governance
# transition whose kee:governedArtifact is the record, or by a revision linked
# with prov:wasRevisionOf, as the adopting profile chooses. Mapping behaviour:
# no generic https://w3id.org/kee/lifecycle# value maps to any concept here.
# Supported never had a defined meaning on this axis; a legacy read is reported
# as a review status not stated in this scheme, never as Accepted.
#
# Labels shared with other schemes do not establish equivalence (Section 9.2).
# Proposed, Rejected, Withdrawn and Superseded share labels with concepts of
# the Assertion and Decision lifecycle schemes and are not asserted equivalent,
# close or related to them. The scheme asserts no external mapping.

grlife:GovernanceRecordReviewStatusScheme
  a skos:ConceptScheme ;
  skos:prefLabel "KEE Governance Record Review Status Scheme"@en ;
  dcterms:identifier "kee-governance-record-lifecycle-v0.11.0" ;
  dcterms:publisher "KEE (KnoEdg + Eidos)" ;
  dcterms:description "Canonical scheme for the review status of a governance record: the record's own standing as a record, as accepted or not by the review that governs records of its kind. It is not the state of anything the record describes. Owner: the Governance Transition Profile; adopted for kee:lifecycleState on kee:GovernanceTransitionRecord, kee:ContradictionRecord, kee:ContestedAuthorityClaim and kee:LifecycleCrosswalkMapping. Status: the owning and adopting profiles are Draft / Non-Normative. Closed: a new concept needs a governed decision, which is a MINOR addition; the five concepts are checked by membership on the four adopting classes. Versioning: additions require a governed decision; the scheme defines no transitions. External mappings: none asserted; shared labels with other KEE lifecycle schemes do not establish equivalence (Section 9.2)."@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "The axis carries only the record's acceptance as a record. It MUST NOT carry a dispute's resolution or disposition, a grant's expiry, revocation or suspension, the recorded or target state of a transition or crosswalk, mapping strength, or epistemic standing, confidence, authority or correctness; each of those has its own carrier. No generic https://w3id.org/kee/lifecycle# value maps to a concept of this scheme."@en ;
  dcterms:conformsTo <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/> ;
  skos:hasTopConcept grlife:Proposed, grlife:Accepted, grlife:Rejected, grlife:Withdrawn, grlife:Superseded .

grlife:Proposed
  a skos:Concept ;
  skos:prefLabel "Proposed"@en ;
  skos:definition "The record has been made and submitted for review, and has not yet been accepted, rejected or withdrawn."@en ;
  skos:inScheme grlife:GovernanceRecordReviewStatusScheme ;
  skos:topConceptOf grlife:GovernanceRecordReviewStatusScheme .

grlife:Accepted
  a skos:Concept ;
  skos:prefLabel "Accepted"@en ;
  skos:definition "The record has been accepted, as a record, by the review that governs records of its kind. This says nothing about whether what it records is correct, authorized, resolved or true."@en ;
  skos:inScheme grlife:GovernanceRecordReviewStatusScheme ;
  skos:topConceptOf grlife:GovernanceRecordReviewStatusScheme .

grlife:Rejected
  a skos:Concept ;
  skos:prefLabel "Rejected"@en ;
  skos:definition "Review did not accept the record, for example because it duplicates another record, is malformed, or is not an instance of its kind. A rejection says nothing about what the record describes. Where it rests on a substantive finding, that finding is represented separately."@en ;
  skos:inScheme grlife:GovernanceRecordReviewStatusScheme ;
  skos:topConceptOf grlife:GovernanceRecordReviewStatusScheme .

grlife:Withdrawn
  a skos:Concept ;
  skos:prefLabel "Withdrawn"@en ;
  skos:definition "The party that made the record, or a party acting on its behalf, withdrew it. Withdrawal is not a review outcome."@en ;
  skos:inScheme grlife:GovernanceRecordReviewStatusScheme ;
  skos:topConceptOf grlife:GovernanceRecordReviewStatusScheme .

grlife:Superseded
  a skos:Concept ;
  skos:prefLabel "Superseded"@en ;
  skos:definition "The record has been replaced by another record of the same kind. The replacement SHOULD be linked with dcterms:isReplacedBy."@en ;
  skos:inScheme grlife:GovernanceRecordReviewStatusScheme ;
  skos:topConceptOf grlife:GovernanceRecordReviewStatusScheme .
